 url←GetBaseURL request;host;scheme;secure
⍝ Returns the absolute base URL the outside world uses, for example "https://tatin.dev".
⍝ If the INI file carries a non-empty "CONFIG:BaseURL" then that is returned, no questions
⍝ asked: a server hiding behind a reverse proxy cannot work out on its own what the world
⍝ sees, since the proxy typically talks plain HTTP to Tatin even when it serves HTTPS itself.
⍝ Otherwise the URL is compiled from the request: "x-forwarded-proto" is honoured for the
⍝ benefit of proxies that send it, and "CONFIG:Secure" decides when they don't.
⍝ Returns an empty vector in case the request does not carry a "host" header.
 url←⊃'' G.INI.Get'CONFIG:BaseURL'
 url↓⍨←-'/'=¯1↑url                                      ⍝ A trailing slash would end up doubled
 :If 0=≢url
     :If 0<≢host←'host'GetFromHeaders request.Headers
         :If 0=≢scheme←'x-forwarded-proto'GetFromHeaders request.Headers
             secure←⊃0 G.INI.Get'CONFIG:Secure'
             scheme←'http','s'/⍨1=secure
         :EndIf
         url←scheme,'://',host
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
⍝Done
